{"id": 10, "ts": 1780456683.9831488, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 1, "agent": "emily_brooks", "message": "I\u2019m inclined to back Sarah\u2019s preference for **Candidate\u202fC** as our leading option.  James just flagged a serious crew\u2011cooperation problem for Candidate\u202fB \u2013 \u201cmakes nasty remarks about his colleagues\u201d \u2013 which directly undermines the collaborative cockpit environment we need, especially on long\u2011haul flights.  While B is very conscientious, handles stress well, and has strong weather\u2011assessment and computer skills, that interpersonal weakness outweighs those strengths in a safety\u2011critical role.\nCandidate\u202fC, on the other hand, demonstrates rapid, correct decision\u2011making and excellent attention to detail, both vital for international operations.  Although C struggles with communicating ideas and is seen as egocentric, his stated priority of putting concern for others above everything suggests a willingness to support the crew, and his attention skills compensate for some communication gaps.  Given the current evidence, C\u2019s decision quality and attentiveness give him the strongest overall fit, provided we later verify his stress resilience and openness to feedback.\nThus, I vote for **Candidate\u202fC** at this stage, while we continue to probe the remaining criteria for all candidates."}
