{"id": 19, "ts": 1780456745.7914488, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 2, "agent": "james_carter", "message": "I\u2019m still inclined to recommend Candidate\u202fC.\u202fTheir ability to make correct decisions quickly, stay calm in a crisis, and understand complicated technology directly hits our top priorities of decision quality, stress resilience, and technical competence.\u202fHowever, the notes about difficulty communicating ideas, being regarded as egocentric, and a lack of willingness to pursue further education raise legitimate concerns about crew cooperation, adaptability, and feedback orientation.\u202fCompared with Candidate\u202fB, who also shows strong stress handling but makes nasty remarks about colleagues, and Candidate\u202fD, whose hot temper and know\u2011it\u2011all attitude could undermine teamwork, C\u2019s communication gaps seem less severe than outright hostility.\u202fIf we can be confident that C\u2019s technical strengths will translate into safe, reliable long\u2011distance operations and that any cooperation issues can be mitigated through training, I believe C remains the best overall fit."}
