{"id": 23, "ts": 1780456777.5085201, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 2, "agent": "emily_brooks", "message": "I appreciate the enthusiasm for Candidate\u202fC\u2019s ability to make quick, correct decisions, which is certainly valuable for long\u2011distance operations. However, I\u2019m increasingly concerned about the reported communication difficulties and egocentric attitude (difficulty communicating ideas, regarded as egocentric, not very willing to further his education). In a cockpit environment, clear, collaborative communication is non\u2011negotiable, and these traits could undermine crew cooperation and safety.\nBy contrast, Candidate\u202fB demonstrates strong stress resilience (handles stress very well), high reliability (very conscientious), and solid technical judgment (good at assessing weather conditions, excellent computer skills). While B is sometimes perceived as pretentious and may adopt the wrong tone, these issues appear less severe than C\u2019s fundamental communication barriers.\nGiven the safety\u2011critical nature of the role, I believe B offers a more balanced profile across the key criteria. I therefore shift my provisional recommendation to Candidate\u202fB, pending any further insights on crew cooperation for the other candidates."}
