{"id": 59, "ts": 1780457013.1605942, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 4, "agent": "sarah_mitchell", "message": "I appreciate James and Emily\u2019s confidence in Candidate\u202fB\u2019s strong stress handling and weather\u2011assessment skills, but I remain convinced that Candidate\u202fC is the better overall fit for our long\u2011distance pilot role.\u202fC\u2019s 100\u202f% reliability and proven ability to make correct decisions quickly directly address our top safety criteria of operational reliability and decision quality. Moreover, C consistently creates a positive atmosphere with the crew, which speaks to crew cooperation and professional communication\u2014essential on long international sectors.\nWhile it is true that C has difficulty communicating ideas, is perceived as egocentric, and is not very willing to pursue further education, these concerns are less detrimental than B\u2019s documented uncooperative and grumpy behavior, which could undermine cockpit teamwork and crew morale.\u202fC\u2019s reliability and decision\u2011making strength outweigh the communication gaps, especially since we can address those through targeted training. Therefore, I continue to recommend Candidate\u202fC."}
